All tasks complete. Summary of what I built in `~/hackachusetts` (no existing `sim/*` file modified, no process touched):

**`sim/ros_pub.py`** — `RosPub` non-blocking ROS 2 facade for the Isaac loop: `pose` (TF `odom→base_link` + `/odom` + decimated `/path` ≥0.15 m, ≤5 Hz), static latched `map→odom` identity on `/tf_static`, `sensor_tf`, `cloud` (PointCloud2 from numpy buffer), `map` (0.10 m voxel downsample via `np.unique`, 400k cap, latched 1 Hz, intensity=z), `image` (rgb8/32FC1, 10 Hz/topic), `mission` (Path + spheres/line/text markers, latched), `defects` (severity-coloured cubes + labels, latched; adapts to the real `defects_gt.json` `type`/int-severity format), `status`, `spin`, `close`.

**`sim/thermal.py`** — honest LWIR approximation (docstring says so). `synth(...)` resizes labels NEAREST before colouring, applies per-class offsets, ±0.6 °C stable spatial noise, `exp(-depth/400)` attenuation, σ≈1 px blur, 0.05 °C NETD, auto-range (2nd/98th pct, 6 °C min span), outputs 640×512. `ironbow(temp, lo, hi)` monotone palette.

**`rviz/inspection.rviz`** — fixed frame `map`, all requested displays, Orbit view (distance 60, pitch 0.5). Validated as well-formed YAML.

**`scripts/rviz.sh`** — sources Jazzy, launches `rviz2 -d <repo>/rviz/inspection.rviz`.

**`tests/`** — `test_ros_pub.py` + `test_thermal.py`, imported by path.

